WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.640
Welfare payments.

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:02.900
When people hear that

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.360
most of us think about poor people lined up

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.960
for food stamps and rent subsidies.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.440
but America’s biggest welfare recipients

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.640
are politically connected corporations,

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:16.100
like America’s sugar industry.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.680
This small group of rich men gets

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.820
billions of dollars in taxpayer subsidies.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:25.540
And yet, they have the nerve to run ads saying we don’t.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:28.540
American farmers don’t get subsidy checks.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:32.400
And America’s multi billion dollar sugar program?

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.539
It costs taxpayers nothing.

00:00:34.539 --> 00:00:35.719
Nothing!

00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:37.829
Their spokesmen go on TV to say:

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:41.040
We are a no cost program, no cost to the taxpayer.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.820
That's absolutely bogus, taxpayers do pay the cost.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:46.500
Ross Marchand of the Taxpayer Protection Alliance

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.680
points out that sugar producers get bailouts

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.300
by us taxpayers whenever sugar prices

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.300
fall below a certain level.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.980
The government will buy sugar

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.940
from the sugar processors

00:00:57.940 --> 00:00:59.820
and sell it to ethanol producers

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.660
at a below market rate.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:02.760
And who's paying the difference?

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.940
Who's footing the bill? U.S. taxpayers.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:06.860
I wanted to interview representatives

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:09.680
of big sugar about their sweet deal.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:11.180
But they would not talk to me.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.560
So, I’ll present their deceptive arguments

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.360
from their ads and public statements.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.280
Depending on others for food

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:20.520
never works out as expected.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:23.600
Big Sugar has the nerve to use images from WWII

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.260
to suggest we’ll have food shortages

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:29.460
if government doesn’t give them a special deal.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:32.200
Does America really want to give foreign countries

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.080
control over its food?

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:35.200
Oh, please!

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.820
Imports increase our supply of food.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:40.840
There are no import restrictions on most other foods

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:43.140
and we have ample supplies of them.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:45.820
Big Sugar also says:

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:48.700
American farmers don’t get subsidy checks

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:52.040
they get loans that are repaid with interest.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:54.820
Has to be repaid with interest!

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.260
Repaid in what?  Sugar?

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:00.780
They actually are allowed to repay in sugar if prices fall

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.220
and taxpayers must pay the difference.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.300
But sugar prices rarely do fall

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.620
because America imposes quotas on

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:10.040
domestic production.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:13.020
And limits how much sugar we can import.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.500
These are Stalin-style price controls

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:19.020
and supply controls and it does not help anyone.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:20.760
Well, it helps big sugar!

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.680
The politically-connected owners

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.380
of the sugar companies collect

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:27.440
several billion extra dollars - from you.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:29.580
At roughly 3 billion a year.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.500
Creighton University economist Diana Thomas explains

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:36.720
why congress never repeals the sugar industry’s scam.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.740
The multi-billion dollar handout costs each of us

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:41.720
maybe 10 or 20 dollars.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:43.520
we’re not going to go to Washington

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:46.380
to lobby against that but -

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:47.680
each American sugar farmer made

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:50.100
roughly 3 million dollars a year extra.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.840
So each of them is willing to spend

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:53.020
a lot of time and money

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.920
making sure the law stays that way.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:58.380
In addition, Americans must pay billions more for food

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:00.640
because Congress restricts imports

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:04.800
of cheaper sugar from places like Brazil and India.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.760
I am prepared to get rid of the sugar program tomorrow

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.740
if the countries we compete against get rid of theirs.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.700
Big sugar’s politicians say,

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:14.840
since other countries foolishly subsidize sugar,

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.600
we must retaliate.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.780
It basically allows our sugar industry to compete

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:21.320
with other countries that are heavily subsidized

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.840
It's only fair to our sugar producers who

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:26.120
don't get subsidized who can't compete with

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:28.100
these subsidized countries.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.200
Is it fair for customers

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.040
to pay double the world rate for sugar?

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.980
Is it fair for taxpayers to have to bail out

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:34.160
a handful of super rich

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:36.160
super-connected sugar processors?

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:36.860
No.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:38.880
So crony capitalists host

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.700
“sweet benefit dinners” while all of us pay more.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:46.540
♪ Domino Sugar makes America smile ♪

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:50.560
The Americans least likely to smile are candy makers.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:51.900
They're the ones hurt most.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:55.180
There's one candy cane producer left in Ohio.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.000
That's absolutely ridiculous.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.660
And look at all those jobs.

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:02.080
People from Akron they need these jobs.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:05.100
20,000 jobs a year lost, says this study.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:08.140
While big sugar pays for ads that say:

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:11.360
Sugar has nothing to hide, that’s because it’s all natural.

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:14.200
These products - they are bad for us!

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.640
Maybe it's good we eat less because they cost more.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:19.540
Well not all sugar products look like that.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:20.980
I mean,  just look at bread.

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:25.240
Bread and beer, yogurt, ketchup and cereal...

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:28.380
The fact that sugar is in everything means that

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:30.020
healthy and unhealthy products alike

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.620
are going to cost more.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.600
And all that money is going to that handful

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:36.920
of rich politically-connected growers and processors.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:40.240
So every time you buy anything made of sugar,

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:42.920
you’re getting ripped off by a clever group

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.540
of businessmen who got your politicians

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:48.520
to pass special laws for sugar.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:51.080
I wish more of you went to Washington, D.C.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:55.060
with a message for big sugar and big government -

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.840
Get out of my life!

